Cell["\<\
To four decimal places the reference gives 0.0654 before the observation and \
0.4411 afterwards. The class-0 posterior probability is 0.5589.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae113357-7824-0f4f-8014-1625726a1e7d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Uncertainty and interval levels", "Subsection",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.8, 0.043137254901960784`, 
   0.00784313725490196],ExpressionUUID->"d9a76efe-b789-a648-b85b-\
ac8bac10568c"],

Cell["\<\
The standard uncertainties are on the probability scale. Changing Level \
changes the interval endpoints. With Measurement set to False, lCProbability \
returns the probability and parameter uncertainty and skips calculation of \
new-result measurement uncertainty. With Measurement set to True (the \
default), Seed and TotalQDraws control the total-Q interval. Their defaults \
are 8271 and 24000 draws.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.004319072462919*^9, 
  4.004319072462919*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6df25a29-6bdd-2e40-98ca-\
29ca065119c6"],

